      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Despite newer lower-profile stent technologies, placing coronary stents may still remain challenging when vessels are extremely tortuous. We describe a case of a tortuous, very largecaliber right coronary with a near-180 degrees switchback \"shepherd's crook\" turn, which could not be stented, and for which double balloon angioplasty was successfully performed."},
